This is how the luckiest game start I ever had finishes with a most
frustrating death: My level 13 monk, AC -10 and 104 HP, was
beginning the castle (having destroyed the drawbridge, and
standing next to the opening with water boots on to beat monsters),
when he became hungry.
So I retreated to the land, away from the water, took a C-ration from
my BoH, ate it, and it was rotten. And then I found myself
surrounded by nasties (including a dragon, a minotaur, and others),
and _paralysed_! They killed me before I had a chance to make any
move (though it took several turns).

I guess the nasties were summoned by one of the lichs in the castle,
but can anyone explain why I was paralysed? I guess it's because
the food was rotten, but I've never noticed this before (maybe
because I usually don't eat when monsters are next to me). Does it
have a chance of happening with all types of food, or only cursed
ones (I didn't know the b/u/c status of my C-ration). How many turns
does it last?

What is most frustrating about this death is that this was the luckiest
game I ever had. By reaching minetown I had found 4 magic lamps
and a co-aligned altar that allowed me to make holy water. This gave
me 3 wishes, that went for the Eye of Aethiopica, an amulet of
reflection (after doing sokoban and finding a BoH), and the Orb of
Fate. I had 104 HP and -10 AC, and was really thinking I could make
something of this char. Bah.

I guess this should be a lesson, but I don't know what the lesson
should be. It's definitely not 'do not eat!', maybe it's 'do not eat
cursed food!'?

